Greg,

I'm using a 166MHz UDB as a Linux server for my home LAN (3 win95
computers) and it works wonderfully.  I can truthfully saw it beats the
snot out of a 486-66, because that's what I run at work as a mail server
(running Linux, naturally).

The cpu runs hot enough to cook breakfast on, so you might want to
consider removing the internal drive and putting it and maybe your cdrom
drive into an external SCSI tower.  I've got a 4 bay tower in which I've
put a cdrom and a 3 GB Seagate Elite series drive (full-height, 5.25
inch beast)

You'd probably also want more than 20 MB of ram, depending on what
you'll be doing with it.  I have 32 in mine and it's not bad.

Hope that helps,
Mike
