X-Sender: hfire@alpha.privatenet.arg
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha


The Alpha 166 UDB is a nice machine, however there are some things you
should know before purchasing one:

1. There is only one PCI slot in the thing, and nobody really knows which
cards work and do not work.

2. The UDB has a  TGA graphics adapter built in. Even though the thing has
2mb of RAM, it only supports 8-bit color (256 colors)

3. It requires true parity, matched ram.

4. The case is VERY compact, and it's unlikely you'll be able to fit a
decent hard drive inside the thing. This means, you must use an
all-external SCSI configuration, which is very expensive. Also be aware
that the back peripheral panel of the UDB is very compact as well, and
depending on the type of cables you plug into it, they may not all fit.
(big bulky D-connectors are a no-no)

I hope this helps





