| on which I can't understand without a description of the hardware (which
| I was unable to find at ftp.figital.com.)

If the modem card can only be set to COM1 or COM2, you need to turn off
the motherboard COM1 or COM2.  Normally a PC bios will let you do this.
The ARC console does not, as far as I can tell.  SRM I don't know about.

It can be easily done by writing the right bytes to the right I/O ports
if you know what multi I/O chip is used on the motherboard.  If it's
National Semi, get a data sheet from www.national.com, if it's SMC,
www.smc.com.  If it's National, I have a pseudobios I wrote for my
Noname that I can send you.  If it's SMC, see SMCInit in bios32.c.



