Michael C. Vergallen (mvergall@alpha.double-barrel.be) wrote:
: Yes I know about that one. I've fixed it by using the following trick :
: edit rc.sysinit....

The proper way of "fixing it" is to tell that you are using ARC clock
when asked in a configuration process.  This will insert a line
like "ARC=true" in /etc/sysconfig/clock (details vary a little between
various releases of Red Hat for Alpha).  This, in turn, will will ensure
that '-A' flag is used on a call to clock to rc.sysinit.  You need, or
not, -u flag as well depending on if your clock is runnig UTC or local
time ("UTC=true|false" in /etc/sysconfig/clock).

Directly editing rc.sysinit is not recommended; you will loose your changes
on the next upgrade.

  Michal



