John Wilson wrote:

> Can anyone direct me to a cheap source for the 32-pin 400 mil DIP 1MBx8
> SRAMs (preferably 15 ns) used for the L2 cache by the AXPpci33?  The best
> I've found so far is $36 for 20 ns parts, and since I need 11 chips that's
> way too much.  Any ideas?

Alliance Semiconductor sells the necessary cache chips for low prices
(AS7C256 or AS7C1024); these are actually 32Kx8 and 128Kx8 for 256Kb
or 1Mb cache, respectively. Get a PDF datasheet from their website for
a list of distributors. I was quoted less than a quarter of your figure.
There is a jumper on the motherboard to select either 15ns or 20ns cache
speed; somebody claimed on USENET that the 15ns 128Kx8 Alliance part
would only work reliably at the 20ns setting, so you might consider
buying either 12ns or 15ns parts to run at 15ns or 20ns, respectively.

http://www.alsc.com/products/prodsram.shtml

