The problem is now solved, due to help from Jay Estabrook.

The cache and P.O.S.T. versions have to be at least B1 and 4.40
respectively to work at 500MHz but the machine was delivered with A1
and 3.70!  We called maintenance and a guy came around with a new
cache.  The P.O.S.T. was on the Web.

Net result:
  Random access is a good bit better for <= 2MB data sizes,
    slightly better for large ones.
  Sequential access is twice as good for <= 2MB data sizes,
    but only half for large ones it seems :-(

